# The residual parquet is a derived artifact of 02_build_oof_residuals.py,
# reproducible from the committed manifest in ../game_latent_state, and
# production history must not inherit it.
oof_gaussian_residuals.parquet

# Fitted-marginal and moment caches. Hundreds of megabytes of pickle that
# belong to the machine that produced them.
*.pkl
*.pickle

# The V2 structural search was screened and not carried, so this directory
# keeps only the evidence that settles the record: the equivalence proof, the
# predictive-SD rejection, the frozen candidate it applies to, the screening
# and temporal artifacts that record why each dial is off, and the compact
# provenance set (factor_spec.json, manifest.json, covariance_diagnostics.json,
# SHA256SUMS.factors.txt) that makes all of it verifiable here.
#
# The research branch that produced them is retired, not merely unmerged. The
# drivers that import a rejected search-space module, those modules themselves
# and the duplicated screening passes are gone from the repository and exist
# only in an offline bundle. Nothing below is retrievable from another branch.
#
# count_bridge.json and repair_control_baseline.json belong to the declined
# count-bridge work; no retained record references either. The earlier
# screening passes are superseded: pass 3 is inner_screening.json byte for
# byte, and pass 1 and 2 are listed in its earlier_pass_artifacts field.
factor_loadings.parquet
count_bridge.json
inner_screening_pass*.json
repair_control_baseline.json
